      "answer": "Perform hand hygiene at five moments: before touching a patient, before a clean or aseptic procedure, after body fluid exposure risk, after touching a patient, and after touching patient surroundings. This guideline applies to all health workers who provide direct patient care in hospitals, clinics and long-term care facilities. It replaces the 2019 edition. Use soap and water when hands are visibly dirty, and after caring for a patient with Clostridioides difficile or norovirus, because alcohol is less effective against spores and non-enveloped viruses.",
